<title>UKRAINE: 2nd Ukraine beet test has 11.4 pct sugar content.</title>
<headline>2nd Ukraine beet test has 11.4 pct sugar content.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The second Ukrainian sugar beet test for 1997 showed an average sugar content of 11.4 percent, down from last year's 12.5 percent, the Agro-Industrial Complex Ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following data for the second test, which was carried out on August 10:</p>
<p>			   2nd 1997 test    Year-ago</p>
<p> Avg sugar content   11.4 pct	   12.5 pct</p>
<p> Beet (root) weight  216 grams	  187 grams</p>
<p> Beets per ha	  82,000	     77,000</p>
<p>Ukraine's 1997 sugar beet crop has been forecast at 27 million tonnes, compared to 24 million tonnes last year.</p>
<p>Refined sugar output has been forecast at 3.26 million tonnes, flat on 1996 levels.</p>
<p>The ministry said the next test would be carried out sometime this week.</p>
<p>--Irene Marushko, Kiev Newsroom +380 44 244-9150</p>
</text>
